Article 18 The sources of cases concerning the supervision of civil actions include:
(1) A party applies to the People's Procuratorate for supervision;
(2) A natural person, legal person, or unincorporated organization other than a party lodges a complaint with the People's Procuratorate;
(3) The People's Procuratorate discovers the matter in the course of performing its duties.

Article 19 In any of the following circumstances, a party may apply to the People's Procuratorate for supervision:
(1) A civil judgment, ruling, or mediation statement that has already taken legal effect falls within the provisions of paragraph 1 of Article 209 of the Civil Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China;
(2) The party considers that a judge has engaged in illegal acts in the civil adjudicative procedure;
(3) The party considers that there are illegal circumstances in civil enforcement activities.

Article 22 The application for supervision as specified in Article 21 of these Rules shall state the following:
(1) the name, gender, age, ethnicity, occupation, work unit, domicile, and valid contact information of the applicant, and the name, domicile, legal representative or principal responsible person's name, position, and valid contact information of a legal person or an unincorporated organization;
(2) the name, gender, work unit, domicile, valid contact information, and other information of other parties, and the name, domicile, responsible person, valid contact information, and other information of a legal person or an unincorporated organization;
(3) the request for supervision;
(4) the specific statutory circumstances and the facts and reasons for applying for supervision.
The applicant shall submit copies of the application for supervision in the number equal to the number of other parties.

Article 26 If a party's application for supervision meets the following conditions, the People's Procuratorate shall accept it:
(1) it conforms to the provisions of Article 19 of these Rules;
(2) the materials provided by the applicant conform to the provisions of Articles 21 through 24 of these Rules;
(3) it falls within the scope of cases accepted by this Procuratorate;
(4) there are no circumstances under which acceptance is refused as provided in these Rules.

Article 27 If a party applies to a People's Procuratorate for supervision pursuant to paragraph 1 of Article 209 of the Civil Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China, and any of the following circumstances exists, the People's Procuratorate shall not accept the application:
(1) the party has not applied to the People's Court for a retrial;
(2) the party's application for retrial exceeds the time limit prescribed by law, unless the delay is not attributable to the party;
(3) the People's Court is in the process of examining the civil retrial application within the statutory period;
(4) the People's Court has already rendered a ruling to retry the case and the retrial has not yet concluded;
(5) the judgment or mediation statement dissolves the marital relationship, unless the party is dissatisfied with the division of property;
(6) the People's Procuratorate has already concluded its examination and made a decision;
(7) the civil judgment, ruling, or mediation statement was made by the People's Court after a retrial pursuant to a protest or a retrial procuratorial recommendation from a People's Procuratorate;
(8) the application for supervision exceeds the time limit prescribed in Article 20 of these Rules;
(9) other circumstances under which acceptance should not be made.

Article 28 If a party believes that there are illegal circumstances in civil adjudication procedures or enforcement activities and applies to a People's Procuratorate for supervision, and any of the following circumstances exists, the People's Procuratorate shall not accept the application:
(1) the law provides that a party may raise an objection, apply for reconsideration, or initiate an action, but the party has not raised an objection, applied for reconsideration, or initiated an action, unless there is a justifiable reason;
(2) after the party has raised an objection, applied for reconsideration, or initiated an action, the People's Court has accepted the matter and is in the process of examining and handling it, unless the court fails to make a decision within the statutory period;
(3) other circumstances under which acceptance should not be made.
If a party applies for supervision over the illegal acts of adjudicators or enforcement personnel, the above paragraph shall not apply.

Article 32 The department in charge of complaint and petition procuratorial work of a People's Procuratorate shall handle a supervision application according to the following circumstances:
(1) if it meets the conditions for acceptance, it shall make a decision to accept in accordance with the provisions of these Rules;
(2) if it does not fall within the scope of cases accepted by this Procuratorate, it shall inform the applicant to apply for supervision to the relevant People's Procuratorate;
(3) if it does not fall within the purview of the People's Procuratorate, it shall inform the applicant to raise the matter with the relevant authority;
(4) if it does not meet the conditions for acceptance and the applicant does not withdraw the supervision application, it may decide not to accept.

Article 37 If a People's Procuratorate discovers in the performance of its duties that a civil case has any of the following circumstances, it shall initiate supervision procedures ex officio:
(1) the case harms national interests or public interests;
(2) an adjudicator or enforcement personnel has engaged in illegal acts such as embezzlement or bribery, engaging in malpractices for personal gain, or perverting the law in rendering judgments;
(3) a party has engaged in acts such as false litigation that disrupt judicial order;
(4) a judgment, ruling, or mediation statement of a civil public interest litigation that has become legally effective, rendered by a People's Court, is indeed erroneous, an adjudicator has engaged in illegal acts in the adjudication procedures, or there are illegal circumstances in the enforcement activities;
(5) follow-up supervision by the People's Procuratorate is required in accordance with relevant provisions;
(6) there are circumstances where supervision is truly necessary, such as having significant social impact.
The initiation of supervision procedures ex officio by a People's Procuratorate over a civil case shall not be limited by whether the party has applied for a retrial.

For a case after the review is completed, a people's procuratorate shall, based on the circumstances, make one of the following decisions:
(1) issuing a procuratorial recommendation for retrial;
(2) requesting a protest or requesting other supervision;
(3) lodging a protest;
(4) issuing a procuratorial recommendation;
(5) terminating the review;
(6) not supporting the supervision application;
(7) affirming the original decision upon review.
For cases accepted by the department responsible for complaints and petition prosecution, the department responsible for civil prosecution shall inform the department responsible for complaints and petition prosecution of the case handling result.

A hearing shall generally be conducted in the following steps:
(1) The prosecutor handling the case introduces the case situation and the issues that need to be heard;
(2) The parties and other participants explain their respective positions on the issues to be heard;
(3) The hearing officers question the parties or other participants;
(4) The moderator adjourns the hearing, and the hearing officers discuss the matters under hearing;
(5) The moderator resumes the hearing, and the hearing officers or their representatives may express opinions based on the case circumstances;
(6) The parties make final statements;
(7) The moderator summarizes the hearing.

Article 62 If the People's Procuratorate has any of the following circumstances due to the need to perform legal supervision duties, it may investigate and verify relevant information from the parties or persons not involved in the case:
(1) The civil judgment, ruling, or mediation document may contain circumstances requiring supervision under the law, which are difficult to determine solely through case file review and examination of existing materials;
(2) There may be illegal conduct by adjudicative personnel in the civil adjudication procedure;
(3) There may be illegal circumstances in civil enforcement activities;
(4) Other circumstances requiring investigation and verification.

Article 63 The People's Procuratorate may take the following investigation and verification measures:
(1) Inquire, obtain, and duplicate relevant evidentiary materials;
(2) Question the parties or persons not involved in the case;
(3) Consult professionals, relevant departments, or industry associations for opinions on specialized issues;
(4) Commission expert evaluation, assessment, or audit;
(5) Inspect physical evidence or the scene;
(6) Other measures necessary to ascertain the facts of the case.
When conducting investigation and verification, the People's Procuratorate shall not take compulsory measures such as restricting personal freedom or sealing, seizing, or freezing property.

Article 64 If any of the following circumstances exist, the People's Procuratorate may inquire, obtain, and duplicate relevant evidentiary materials from banking financial institutions:
(1) National interests or public interests may be harmed;
(2) There may be illegal conduct by adjudicative or enforcement personnel;
(3) It involves a lawsuit as provided for in Article 55 of the Civil Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China;
(4) There is a possibility that a party has forged evidence or maliciously colluded to harm the lawful rights and interests of others.
The People's Procuratorate may, in accordance with relevant regulations, designate procuratorial technical personnel with appropriate qualifications to conduct a specialized review of technical evidence such as expert evaluation opinions in civil action supervision cases, and issue review opinions.

Article 72 If any of the following circumstances exist, the People's Procuratorate may suspend the review:
(1) The natural person applying for supervision has died, and it is necessary to wait for the heir to indicate whether to continue the application for supervision;
(2) The legal person or unincorporated organization applying for supervision has terminated, and the rights and obligations successor has not yet been determined;
(3) The present case must be based on the outcome of another case, but that other case has not yet been concluded;
(4) Other circumstances under which the review may be suspended.
If the review is suspended, a Decision to Suspend Review shall be issued and served on the party. After the cause for suspension is eliminated, the review shall be promptly resumed.

Article 73 If any of the following circumstances exist, the People's Procuratorate shall terminate the review:
(1) The People's Court has already ruled for retrial or has already corrected the illegal conduct;
(2) The applicant withdraws the application for supervision, and it does not harm national interests, public interests, or the lawful rights and interests of others;
(3) The applicant declares in a settlement agreement reached with other parties the waiver of the right to apply for supervision, and it does not harm national interests, public interests, or the lawful rights and interests of others;
(4) The natural person applying for supervision has died, with no heir or the heir waives the application, and no other illegal circumstances requiring supervision are found;
(5) The legal person or unincorporated organization applying for supervision has terminated, with no rights and obligations successor or the successor waives the application, and no other illegal circumstances requiring supervision are found;
(6) It is found that an already accepted case does not meet the acceptance conditions;
(7) For a case where the People's Procuratorate initiates the supervision procedure ex officio, upon review it is determined that no supervision measures are necessary;
(8) Other circumstances under which the review shall be terminated.
If the review is terminated, a Decision to Terminate Review shall be issued; if it is necessary to notify the parties, it shall be served on the parties.

Article 77 Any of the following circumstances shall be determined as "the basic facts determined lack evidence to prove" as provided for in Item (2) of Article 200 of the Civil Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China:
(1) The determined basic facts are not supported by evidence, or the evidence on which the determined basic facts are based is false or lacks probative force;
(2) The evidence on which the determined basic facts are based is illegal;
(3) The determination of the basic facts violates logical reasoning or the rules of daily life;
(4) Other circumstances where the determined basic facts lack evidence to prove.

Article 78 Any of the following circumstances, resulting in an erroneous outcome in the original judgment or ruling, shall be determined as "the application of law is indeed erroneous" as provided for in Item (6) of Article 200 of the Civil Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China:
(1) The law applied is clearly inconsistent with the nature of the case;
(2) The determination of civil liability clearly violates the agreement of the parties or legal provisions;
(3) The law applied has already ceased to have effect or has not yet come into force;
(4) The provisions on the retroactive effect of the law are violated;
(5) The rules for the application of law are violated;
(6) The legislative intent is clearly contradicted;
(7) Other circumstances involving erroneous application of law.

Article 79 Any of the following circumstances shall be determined as "the composition of the adjudicative organization is illegal" as provided for in Item (7) of Article 200 of the Civil Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China:
(1) A case that should be tried by a collegial panel is tried by a single judge;
(2) People's assessors participate in the trial of a case at second instance;
(3) A case on retrial or remanded for retrial does not have a separate collegial panel formed;
(4) The persons trying the case do not have adjudicative qualifications;
(5) Other circumstances where the adjudicative organization or personnel are illegal.

Article 80 Any of the following circumstances shall be deemed as 'violating legal provisions and depriving a party of the right to debate' as specified in Item (9) of Article 200 of the Civil Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China:
(1) Disallowing or severely restricting the party from exercising the right to debate;
(2) Failing to hold a hearing when a hearing shall be held;
(3) Violating legal provisions in serving a copy of the bill of prosecution or a copy of the bill of appeal, thereby causing the party to be unable to exercise the right to debate;
(4) Other circumstances of illegally depriving a party of the right to debate.

Article 81 If a local people's procuratorate at any level discovers that an effective civil judgment or ruling of a people's court at the same level falls under any of the following circumstances, it may submit a procuratorial recommendation for retrial to the people's court at the same level:
(1) There is new evidence sufficient to overturn the original judgment or ruling;
(2) The basic facts found in the original judgment or ruling lack evidentiary support;
(3) The main evidence for the facts found in the original judgment or ruling is forged;
(4) The main evidence for the facts found in the original judgment or ruling was not cross-examined;
(5) For the main evidence needed for adjudication of the case, the party was unable to collect it due to objective reasons and made a written application to the people's court for investigation and collection, but the people's court failed to investigate and collect it;
(6) The composition of the adjudicative body is illegal, or a judicial officer who shall recuse according to law fails to recuse;
(7) A person without capacity to conduct litigation is not represented by a legal representative, or a party that shall participate in the action fails to participate due to reasons not attributable to the party or the party's litigation agent;
(8) Violating legal provisions and depriving a party of the right to debate;
(9) Rendering a default judgment without service of a summons;
(10) The original judgment or ruling omits or exceeds the claims of the action;
(11) The legal instrument on which the original judgment or ruling is based has been revoked or modified.

Article 82 If a case that meets the provisions of Article 81 of these Rules falls under any of the following circumstances, the local people's procuratorate at any level shall generally refer the matter to the next higher people's procuratorate for a protest:
(1) The judgment or ruling was made after a retrial by the people's court at the same level;
(2) The judgment or ruling was made after discussion by the adjudicative committee of the people's court at the same level.

Article 83 If a local people's procuratorate at any level discovers that an effective civil judgment or ruling of a people's court at the same level falls under any of the following circumstances, it shall generally refer the matter to the next higher people's procuratorate for a protest:
(1) The original judgment or ruling definitely errs in the application of law;
(2) The judicial officer, when adjudicating the case, engaged in embezzlement or bribery, committed favoritism or fraud, or rendered a judgment in violation of the law.

Article 96 The duties of procuratorial personnel appearing in the retrial court are:
(1) To read the Protest Letter;
(2) To present and explain the evidence obtained through investigation by the people's procuratorate;
(3) At the conclusion of the trial, with the permission of the presiding judge, to express opinions on legal supervision;
(4) To record instances of violation of procedural rules during the court trial.
If procuratorial personnel find that the trial activities are illegal, they shall, after adjournment or conclusion of the trial, submit a procuratorial recommendation in the name of the people's procuratorate.
The procuratorial personnel appearing in court shall attend the entire trial.

Article 98 The adjudication procedures as specified in paragraph 3 of Article 208 of the Civil Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China include:
(1) ordinary procedure of first instance;
(2) summary procedure;
(3) procedure of second instance;
(4) special procedure;
(5) trial supervision procedure;
(6) supervision procedure;
(7) public summons and exhortation procedure;
(8) special procedure for maritime litigation;
(9) bankruptcy procedure.

Article 100 Where a People's Procuratorate discovers any of the following circumstances in the civil adjudication procedure of the people's court at the same level, it shall issue a procuratorial recommendation to the people's court at the same level:
(1) a judgment or ruling is indeed erroneous but is not suitable for correction through retrial procedures;
(2) the mediation violates the principle of voluntariness or the content of the mediation agreement violates the law;
(3) the conditions for prosecution and acceptance provided by law are met, but the case should have been docketed and is not docketed;
(4) the adjudication procedure applied in hearing the case is erroneous;
(5) the preservation or advance execution violates the provisions of the law;
(6) the payment order violates the provisions of the law;
(7) the suspension or termination of the action violates the provisions of the law;
(8) the statutory time limit for adjudication is violated;
(9) compulsory measures against a party, such as a fine or detention, for obstructing civil actions violate the provisions of the law;
(10) service violates the provisions of the law;
(11) other circumstances that violate the provisions of the law.

Article 106 Where a People's Procuratorate discovers any of the following circumstances in the enforcement activities of a people's court, it shall issue a procuratorial recommendation to the people's court at the same level:
(1) there are illegal or erroneous circumstances in enforcement review activities such as deciding whether to accept, transferring enforcement jurisdiction, and reviewing and handling enforcement objections, reconsiderations, petitions, etc.;
(2) there are illegal or erroneous circumstances in enforcement implementation activities such as property investigation, control, disposal, delivery and distribution, as well as fines, detention, credit disciplinary measures, etc.;
(3) there are circumstances such as passive enforcement or delayed enforcement;
(4) other illegal or erroneous enforcement circumstances.

Article 112 Where the department responsible for case management discovers any of the following circumstances in the case-handling activities of the procuratorate, it shall promptly propose corrective opinions:
(1) the preparation and use of legal documents do not comply with laws and relevant provisions;
(2) the provisions on case-handling time limits are violated;
(3) the litigation rights of parties or litigation agents are infringed;
(4) legal supervision duties are not performed according to law regarding illegal acts in civil adjudication activities and enforcement activities;
(5) other circumstances where corrective opinions should be proposed.
If the circumstances are minor, an oral reminder may be given; if the circumstances are relatively serious, a Notice on Case Process Monitoring shall be sent to remind the case-handling department to promptly ascertain the situation and make corrections; if the circumstances are serious, a report shall be simultaneously made to the chief procurator.
After receiving the Notice on Case Process Monitoring, the case-handling department shall, within ten days, provide a written reply on the verification results to the department responsible for case management.

Article 117 Where a People's Procuratorate discovers that a people's court has any of the following circumstances in multiple civil cases of the same type, it may issue a procuratorial recommendation:
(1) inconsistent application of law to similar issues;
(2) the same type of error in the application of law;
(3) other similar illegal acts.
Where a People's Procuratorate discovers that the work system, management methods, or work procedures of a relevant unit are illegal or improper and need to be corrected or improved, it may issue a procuratorial recommendation.

Article 124 In any of the following circumstances, the People's Procuratorate may, in accordance with relevant provisions, supervise again or request the People's Procuratorate at a higher level to supervise:
(1) the judgment, ruling, or mediation agreement made by the People's Court in hearing a civil protest case still contains obvious errors;
(2) the People's Court fails to handle and reply in writing to the procuratorial recommendation within the prescribed time limit;
(3) the handling result of the People's Court regarding the procuratorial recommendation is erroneous.

Article 126 Where a party considers that a decision of the People's Procuratorate at the same level not to support an application for supervision regarding a legally effective civil judgment, ruling, or mediation agreement of the People's Court contains an obvious error, the party may, within one year from the date the decision not to support the application for supervision is made, apply to the People's Procuratorate at the next higher level for one review. The department responsible for complaints and prosecution, after preliminary verification, discovers that there may be any of the following circumstances, may transfer the case to the department responsible for civil procuratorial work of that procuratorate for review and handling:
(1) there is new evidence sufficient to overturn the original judgment or ruling;
(2) there is evidence proving that the main evidence for the facts found in the original judgment or ruling was forged;
(3) the legal instrument based on which the original judgment or ruling was made has been revoked or modified;
(4) there is evidence proving that the adjudicators engaged in embezzlement, bribery, favoritism, or perversion of law in adjudicating the case;
(5) there is evidence proving that the procuratorial personnel engaged in embezzlement, bribery, favoritism, or abuse of power in handling the case;
(6) other circumstances where review is indeed necessary.
After review, if the department responsible for civil procuratorial work considers that the decision of the lower-level People's Procuratorate not to support the supervision application is erroneous, it shall revoke the decision in the name of the People's Procuratorate and file a protest according to law; if it considers that there is no error, it shall decide to maintain the decision upon review, and shall prepare a Review Decision Letter and send it to the applicant.
The People's Procuratorate at a higher level may, ex officio, review a case in which a lower-level People's Procuratorate made a decision not to support an application for supervision regarding a legally effective civil judgment, ruling, or mediation agreement made by a People's Court at the same level.
The time limit for review of a reviewed case shall be handled by reference to the provisions of Article 52, paragraph 1 of these Rules.
